-- title:
--   Smooth-point stalks from the affine chart at q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=3$ and a level $M'$, nonzero and not divisible by $q$, together with an auxiliary prime $\ell_g$ satisfying $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$, and let $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $=\kappa(j,j_{M'})$ over $\kappa$, assumed by `hW` to consist exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa\to$ residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen } \kappa\,M')$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`; and let $s\in W$ be one of them. The inclusion `hle` expresses that the base-changed modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $=$ `laurentBaseChange`$(\overline{\mathbb Q},$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`$)$ is contained in $F:=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar`$(q^2M',$ `levelH q M'`$)$, both taken inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` with surjective residue map onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on constants, together with a map on places preserving degrees and orders), and `hR₀` requires that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` belongs to `R₀.integers` and that its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   The base data are a subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ containing $\mathbb Q$, an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, and the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` that $A\cap k_0$ (formally $A$ pulled back along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` that every element of $A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Rigidifying data are a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an element $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b=\bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$, and $\varpi_b\neq 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   With $F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is an implication between two packages of conditions on a pair $(F_0,W_0)$, where $F_0$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq F$ and $W_0$ a valuation subring of $F_0$. The hypothesis package consists of:
--
--   (K1) $\operatorname{adjoin}_{k_0}(\overline{\mathbb Q})\sqcup F_0=\top$, i.e. $F_0$ together with the constants generates $F$ over $k_0$; (K2) for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$; (K3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; (K4) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; (K5) there is $t\in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ then every coefficient of $p$ has image in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; (LD) for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, if $g$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ (the image of `jq`) has non-negative order, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $g$ in $F$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; (EQ) for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into itself and preserves membership in $W_0$; (LI) for every finite-dimensional intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, any family $c_0,\dots,c_{m-1}\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ remains linearly independent over the compositum $\operatorname{adjoin}_{k_0}(K')\sqcup F_0$: if elements $a_i$ of that compositum satisfy $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$, then all $a_i=0$;
--
--   (AC) the affine chart: there exist a subring $B$ of $F$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that the structure map is the inclusion of $A_b\subseteq K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ into $F$; $B$ is contained in the compositum $\operatorname{adjoin}_{k_0}(K_b)\sqcup F_0$, and every element of that compositum is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $B$ is contained in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that element, in the sense that $f\in W_0$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$; the image of $j$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and, for every algebra structure of $\mathbb F_{q^2}=$ `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (two-variable polynomials modulo `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field of $C_s$ acting on the Drinfeld function field) with $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, with kernel $\varpi_b B$, compatible with the reduction $A_b\to\kappa$, such that every element of the target is a quotient $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$, such that the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements lying in the image of `CoordRing q κ` in the Drinfeld function field, and such that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathtt{redQ } q\,\gamma,1)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) one has $\rho(\mathtt{levelAutBar } q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}f)=\mathtt{hFunctionFieldAction}$ at that element applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   Under (K1)–(K5), (LD), (EQ), (LI) and (AC), the conclusion is: the eight clauses (K1), (K2), (K3), (K4), (K5), (LD), (EQ), (LI) hold verbatim as above, and moreover, for every field $F_{SS}$ that is an algebra over $\kappa$ and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $F_{SS}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ with surjective residue map onto $F_{SS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on constants, and normalised by the clause `exists_smul_mem`) such that $R$ induces $W_0$ on $F_0$ (for $f\in F_0$: $f\in$ `R.integers` iff $f\in W_0$), the following two statements hold.
--
--   First, the Drinfeld identification of the residue field: for every algebra structure of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ on $\kappa$, every witness that `CoordRing q κ` is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and an isomorphism $e:F_{SS}\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) of $\kappa$-algebras with $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ for which `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and for which $(\mathtt{redQ } q\,\gamma,1)\in$ `hSubgroup q`, the automorphism `R.resAut` induced on $F_{SS}$ by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` corresponds under $e$ to `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at that element.
--
--   Second, there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$, a family of subrings $S_Q\subseteq F$ indexed by places $Q$ of $F_{SS}$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q:A_b[X]\to S_Q$, ring homomorphisms $\chi_Q:S_Q\to\kappa$, and sets $D_Q$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that: $\#N=q+1$; there is a subring $B$ of $F$ contained in `R.integers`, contained in $S_Q$ for every $Q\notin N$, such that every $z\in F_{SS}$ lying in the valuation subring of each $Q\notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$; and for every $Q\notin N$ the following hold: the image of $A_b$ in $F$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for $a\in A_b$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q X)=0$; $S_Q$ carries a local ring structure for which the kernel of $\chi_Q$ is the maximal ideal; $S_Q$ is contained in the compositum $\operatorname{adjoin}_{k_0}(K_b)\sqcup F_0$ and every element of that compositum is a quotient of two elements of $S_Q$ with non-zero denominator; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and of essentially finite type; $S_Q$ is contained in `R.integers`, and an element of $S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` precisely when it is divisible by $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$; for every $f\in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q X$ lies in `R.integers` and has order $1$ at $Q$; and $D_Q$ consists exactly of the places $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are rational, for which every $f\in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and for which, for every $f\in S_Q$, the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f)=0$. Furthermore the discs are pairwise disjoint: if $Q,Q'\notin N$ and some place $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q=Q'$; the discs avoid the cusps: for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_Q$ the order of $j$ at $P$ is non-negative; and the whole configuration is level-equivariant: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves `R.integers`, and every place $Q$ of $F_{SS}$, one has $\mathtt{R.resAut }\tau\cdot Q\in N$ if and only if $Q\in N$, and if $Q\notin N$ then `smulDisc τ` $(D_Q)=\{P:\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D_Q\}$ equals $D_{\mathtt{R.resAut }\tau\cdot Q}$.
--
--   This is the step, for the prime $q=3$ at an auxiliary level divisible by a prime $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$, which converts an affine chart of the supersingular component of the descended regular model into the data attached to the component itself: the identification of the residue field of a regular prolongation with a quotient of the Drinfeld function field $xy^q-x^qy=1$, and, at each reduced place off the $q+1$ ends, an étale coordinate, a residue character and a residue disc of rational places, disjoint, cusp-free and permuted by the level automorphisms. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart) in the construction of semistable models of modular curves of full level at $3$.
